From b5e49613098e5e45c5b6cb83dff338cf2d56e9a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Amitabh Pandey <amitabh@elimentary.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 04:33:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Play footage in real time instead of seeking per frame

The preview seeked the hidden video element to the playhead on every
timeline tick and awaited `seeked` before redrawing, so each animation
frame cost a keyframe-to-target decode and uploaded videos stuttered.

- While the timeline plays, the element now plays on its own (looping,
  re-synced only on >250ms drift) and the sheet re-samples once per new
  video frame.
- Paused/scrub still seeks to the exact frame, but concurrent seeks
  coalesce to the newest target.
- An exact seek holds live playback briefly so MP4 export, which seeks
  frame by frame, is never restarted between frames.
- Reuse one sampling OffscreenCanvas instead of allocating per frame.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BzcEuDYMjn12A8YtyMv3Bb
